A particle of mass m moves on a straight line with its velocity increasing with distance according to the equation
v = \alpha \sqrt{x}
, where \(\alpha\) is a constant. The total work done by all the forces applied on the particle during its displacement from x = 0 to x = d, will be :

questions.explanation:
